    "Navy has its own set of standards that use a maximum body fat percentage of 23% for men and 34% for women for ages 18-21, with different standards for different age groups.",
    "Air Force has a maximum body fat percentage of 20% for men and 28% for women for ages 17-29.",
    "Marine Corps standards dictate 18% body fat for males and 26% for females for new recruits, though these percentages change with age.",
    "After measuring his neck and waist and inputting his data, he receives an estimated body fat measurement of 23%.",
    "If you need to drop 5% body fat to meet Army standards, aim to lose about 1% per week rather than attempting to crash diet and lose it all in seven days."
